cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QUARTIC2D in research, please cite the software release."
title: "QUARTIC2D: Quadrature for Radial Tetra-center Interaction Coefficients in 2D"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  QUARTIC2D is a Python package for efficient evaluation of interaction matrix
  elements between localized two-dimensional fields with radially symmetric
  interaction kernels. It is built on top of PETAL2D and combines angular
  harmonic decompositions with radial Hankel-transform and interaction
  backends including Simpson and Gauss-Legendre quadrature, Ogata quadrature,
  and FFTLog.
authors:
  - family-names: "Santacruz"
    given-names: "Alex"
keywords:
  - scientific computing
  - Hankel transform
  - numerical quadrature
  - two-dimensional materials
  - interaction matrix elements
  - condensed matter physics
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantumArtificer/quartic2d"
url: "https://github.com/QuantumArtificer/quartic2d"
license: MIT
